      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Krea 2 Turbo — 4-Step Distillation LoRA\n\nKrea 2 Turbo normally needs **8 steps**. With this community-trained LoRA it runs at **4** — roughly a 1.6-1.8x speedup end to end — while keeping most of the quality.\n\nLoRA by **lvladikov**: https://huggingface.co/lvladikov/Krea2-Turbo-Distill-4step-LoRA\n\n### Files (this workflow's defaults)\n| file | put it in |\n| --- | --- |\n| `krea2_turbo_fp8.safetensors` (or a GGUF quant) | `models/diffusion_models/` (GGUF → `models/unet/`) |\n| `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` | `models/text_encoders/` |\n| `qwen_image_vae.safetensors` | `models/vae/` |\n| `krea2_turbo_4step_rank_64_lora_latest_comfyui.safetensors` | `models/loras/` |\n\nThe first three are the standard Krea 2 companions from [Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2). Set the CLIPLoader **type to `krea2`**.\n\n### Base model is your choice\nThe LoRA is applied on top of the diffusion model by ComfyUI's loader, so it works the same on any Krea 2 Turbo build. This workflow ships an **FP8** default (NVIDIA) plus a **GGUF loader path** for lower VRAM — switch between them with the model Switcher. Use whichever fits your hardware and leave the rest of the workflow alone.\n\n### Settings that matter\n- **steps 4**, **cfg 1.0** (Turbo is CFG-free), sampler **euler**, scheduler **simple**\n- LoRA strength **1.0**\n- The negative is a `ConditioningZeroOut` — at cfg 1.0 it isn't evaluated, so nothing goes in it\n- To compare against stock Turbo: set steps to 8 and bypass the LoRA node (Ctrl+B)\n\n### Work in progress\nThe LoRA is an ongoing training run. The workflow points at `..._latest_comfyui.safetensors`, which always holds the newest published checkpoint — just re-download that one file to stay current, no workflow edit needed. Numbered copies are kept on the repo if you want to pin a specific checkpoint. Full details and evaluation on lvladikov's repo."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Krea 2 Turbo — 4-Step Distillation LoRA\n\nKrea 2 Turbo normally needs **8 steps**. With this community-trained LoRA it runs at **4** — roughly a 1.6-1.8x speedup end to end — while keeping most of the quality.\n\nLoRA by **lvladikov**: https://huggingface.co/lvladikov/Krea2-Turbo-Distill-4step-LoRA\n\n### Files (this workflow's defaults)\n| file | put it in |\n| --- | --- |\n| `krea2_turbo_fp8.safetensors` (or a GGUF quant) | `models/diffusion_models/` (GGUF → `models/unet/`) |\n| `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` | `models/text_encoders/` |\n| `qwen_image_vae.safetensors` | `models/vae/` |\n| `krea2_turbo_4step_rank_64_lora_latest_comfyui.safetensors` | `models/loras/` |\n\nThe first three are the standard Krea 2 companions from [Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2). Set the CLIPLoader **type to `krea2`**.\n\n### Base model is your choice\nThe LoRA is applied on top of the diffusion model by ComfyUI's loader, so it works the same on any Krea 2 Turbo build. This workflow ships an **FP8** default (NVIDIA) plus a **GGUF loader path** for lower VRAM — switch between them with the model Switcher. Use whichever fits your hardware and leave the rest of the workflow alone.\n\n### Settings that matter\n- **steps 4**, **cfg 1.0** (Turbo is CFG-free), sampler **euler**, scheduler **simple**\n- LoRA strength **1.0**\n- The negative is a `ConditioningZeroOut` — at cfg 1.0 it isn't evaluated, so nothing goes in it\n- To compare against stock Turbo: set steps to 8 and bypass the LoRA node (Ctrl+B)\n\n### Work in progress\nThe LoRA is an ongoing training run. The workflow points at `..._latest_comfyui.safetensors`, which always holds the newest published checkpoint — just re-download that one file to stay current, no workflow edit needed. Numbered copies are kept on the repo if you want to pin a specific checkpoint. Full details and evaluation on lvladikov's repo."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
